libdnet-stripped's pre-generated configure probes for Linux PF_PACKET with a
nested function inside main() (`int foo() { return ETH_P_ALL; }`), a GNU C
extension clang rejects ("function definition is not allowed here"). Under the
engine the probe fails to compile, answers "no", and configure aborts with
"Ethernet support not found for this system". Use the form the sibling arp
probe already uses, so the macro is referenced instead of called. Inert on
darwin (Linux-only probe).

--- a/libdnet-stripped/configure
+++ b/libdnet-stripped/configure
@@ -15219,7 +15219,7 @@
 int
 main (void)
 {
-int foo() { return ETH_P_ALL; }
+int foo = ETH_P_ALL;
   ;
   return 0;
 }
